# Star Trek Galaxies -- sprites for the Trek event pictures our archaeological
# sites use.
#
# A SECOND new file beside interface/stg_event_pictures.gfx rather than an
# extension of it, because the two databases are read by two different checks
# and a session that breaks one should not have to read the other. Everything
# in the sibling's header applies here unchanged:
#
#   TWO SPRITES PER PICTURE -- interface/eventpictures.gfx says "the Situation
#   Log automatically uses sprites with the _nomask suffix if available", and a
#   dig site lives in the situation log, so the _nomask twin is not optional
#   decoration here the way it nearly is for an anomaly popup.
#
#   The art is 620x264 or a 9315x264 animation strip in .source/; `target:
#   family` on gfx/event_pictures in vendor.yml re-cuts it to vanilla's 450x150
#   at harvest, freezing frame 0 of a strip. Without that this file is decision
#   42's defect: UIOD's eventwindow.gui draws at scale = 1.5 inside a 693x239
#   frame, so 620x264 art renders 930x396.
#   See .docs/decisions/69-event-picture-families.md.
#
# ALL 27 WERE LOOKED AT AS THE BUILD WILL CUT THEM -- frame 0, centre-cropped
# to 450x150 -- and eleven candidates were rejected on what that crop showed:
# four TAS-animated frames, three close-ups of a named character's face, two
# near-featureless gradients and two too dark to read at this size. A filename
# cannot make that call. Same standard as
# .docs/decisions/70-trek-anomalies.md set for the anomaly pictures.
#
# NONE OF THE 27 IS ALREADY DECLARED by the anomalies' file, which is a
# constraint and not a coincidence: theChase, undergroundTunnels, stone_of_gol
# and ancientCapsule1 were all first choices here and all four are already
# spent on an anomaly, so the sites took stone_of_gol_1/_3 and ancientCapsule2
# and found other art for the caves. One picture, one subject.
#
# See .docs/decisions/71-trek-archaeology.md

